node_modules
dist
.env
*.local

# `.env` holds whatever a developer needs locally and stays out. `.env.production`
# holds only the public API URL, and it is committed on purpose: leaving that to a
# dashboard variable is how the deployed app ended up pointing at the wrong path
# twice. It must not be given secrets -- Vite inlines every VITE_ value into the
# bundle, so anything in here is public the moment it ships.
!.env.production
